The files in levels/ and wordlists/ are an adaptation of the material listed
below. Changes made: words were selected, filtered (proper nouns,
abbreviations, foreign words, offensive words removed), converted to upper
case, ranked by frequency and combined into puzzle levels. No frequency values
are included.

1. wordfreq 3.1.1
   Robyn Speer et al., https://github.com/rspeer/wordfreq
   Data licensed CC BY-SA 4.0 (code Apache 2.0, not included).
   Citation: Robyn Speer. (2022). rspeer/wordfreq: v3.0 (v3.0.2). Zenodo.
   https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7199437
   wordfreq contains data from:
   - Google Books Ngrams, http://books.google.com/ngrams
   - Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia, http://www.wikipedia.org
   - the Leeds Internet Corpus, University of Leeds Centre for Translation
     Studies, http://corpus.leeds.ac.uk/list.html
   - ParaCrawl, https://paracrawl.eu
   - OPUS OpenSubtitles 2018, http://opus.nlpl.eu/OpenSubtitles.php, whose
     data originates from the OpenSubtitles project,
     http://www.opensubtitles.org/
   - the SUBTLEX word lists (SUBTLEX-US, SUBTLEX-UK, SUBTLEX-CH, SUBTLEX-DE,
     SUBTLEX-NL) created by Marc Brysbaert et al. SUBTLEX is freely available
     data: http://crr.ugent.be/programs-data/subtitle-frequencies
   Used for: frequency ranking of English and Czech words.

2. Universal Dependencies, release 2.18, https://universaldependencies.org/
   Licensed CC BY-SA 4.0.
   - UD_Czech-CAC  - Barbora Hladká, Daniel Zeman
     https://github.com/UniversalDependencies/UD_Czech-CAC
   - UD_Czech-CLTT - Barbora Hladká, Daniel Zeman, Martin Popel
     https://github.com/UniversalDependencies/UD_Czech-CLTT
   - UD_Czech-PUD  - Václava Kettnerová, Jan Hajič jr., Silvie Cinková,
     Zdeňka Urešová, Milan Straka, Jan Hajič, Jaroslava Hlaváčová,
     Daniel Zeman
     https://github.com/UniversalDependencies/UD_Czech-PUD
   Used for: Czech lemmas, parts of speech, proper-noun and abbreviation
   filtering.

3. 12dicts (2of12id, 3esl, abbr), alt12dicts 2020.12.07, by Alan Beale
   Public domain. http://wordlist.aspell.net/12dicts/
   Used for: English headwords and filtering.

4. ENABLE word list (enable1) - public domain.
   Used for: English spelling check.
